---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const faqSchema = {
 "@context": "https://schema.org",
 "@type": "FAQPage",
 "mainEntity": [
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What does 'without downtime' actually mean?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "No user sees an error page. Some users hit the old server, others hit the new one during the propagation window, but both serve content."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Can I change multiple records at once?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Yes for unrelated records (a web A record and an MX record). For related records (several A records for the same service), change them together."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What if I need to roll back?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Re-create the old records from your backup. Propagation of the rollback takes one more TTL cycle."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Does changing DNS affect email?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Only if you change MX records. A/CNAME changes affect web traffic but not email routing (unless the mail host IP changes too)."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "How do I know propagation is complete?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "The propagation checker shows all resolvers returning the same answer. When they agree, propagation is done."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What is the safest day to change DNS?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Any day, if you follow the TTL procedure. Avoid Friday afternoons: if something goes wrong, support teams are unavailable over the weekend."
   }
  }
 ]
}
---
<BaseLayout
  title="How to Change DNS Records Without Downtime | PromptDNS"
  description="change dns records safely without downtime"
  schema={[faqSchema]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/dns/" class="hover:text-accent">DNS Guide</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">Change DNS Records Safely</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">How to Change DNS Records Without Downtime</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">The safe record-change procedure: lower TTL, verify the new value, watch propagation, and keep the old path alive throughout.</p>
    <div class="rich-text mt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">The procedure</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li class="leading-relaxed"><strong class="text-ink">T-24 hours: Lower TTL</strong> to 300 on every record you’ll change. This is the single most important step.</li><li class="leading-relaxed"><strong class="text-ink">T-24 hours: Back up</strong> all records (export or capture with the record lookup).</li><li class="leading-relaxed"><strong class="text-ink">T-0: Make the change</strong> in your DNS panel. Verify the new value with the record lookup immediately.</li><li class="leading-relaxed"><strong class="text-ink">T+0 to T+TTL: Monitor</strong> with the propagation checker. Resolvers disagree during this window: that’s expected.</li><li class="leading-relaxed"><strong class="text-ink">T+TTL: Confirm and restore</strong> TTLs to 3600 once all resolvers return the new value.</li></ul>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">The three rules</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li class="leading-relaxed">One change at a time: stacking changes makes diagnosis impossible.</li><li class="leading-relaxed">Never delete before you add: create the new record, verify, then remove the old.</li><li class="leading-relaxed">Keep the old server running: cached traffic still arrives at the old address for one TTL cycle.</li></ul>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What does 'without downtime' actually mean?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">No user sees an error page. Some users hit the old server, others hit the new one during the propagation window, but both serve content.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Can I change multiple records at once?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Yes for unrelated records (a web A record and an MX record). For related records (several A records for the same service), change them together.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What if I need to roll back?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Re-create the old records from your backup. Propagation of the rollback takes one more TTL cycle.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Does changing DNS affect email?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Only if you change MX records. A/CNAME changes affect web traffic but not email routing (unless the mail host IP changes too).</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How do I know propagation is complete?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">The propagation checker shows all resolvers returning the same answer. When they agree, propagation is done.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What is the safest day to change DNS?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Any day, if you follow the TTL procedure. Avoid Friday afternoons: if something goes wrong, support teams are unavailable over the weekend.</p></details></div>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Related</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-2"><li><a href="/what-is-ttl-in-dns/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">TTL explained →</a></li><li><a href="/dns-migration-checklist/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">DNS migration checklist →</a></li><li><a href="/dns-propagation-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">Propagation checker →</a></li></ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
